          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Borel measures are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measures"} measures
            on the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Borel σ-algebra
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Borel+%CF%83-algebra"} ?
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Borel measure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a (countably additive) measure on the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Borel σ-algebra
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Borel+%CF%83-algebra"} ?
            of the topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A
            %strong Baire measure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a (countably additive) measure on the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Baire σ-algebra
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Baire+%CF%83-algebra"} ?
            of the topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon measure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a Borel measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+subset"} Borel subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\subset X
            and any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt0
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset B
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mu|(B\setminus K)\lt\epsilon
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mu|
            denotes the total
            %span.newWikiWord
              variation
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/variation"} ?
            of the measure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            Borel measures are uniquely determined by their values on open subsets, and are closely related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuations"} continuous valuations
            on the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            A measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            on a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong tight
            if for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt0
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mu|(A)\lt\epsilon
            for any
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subset X\setminus K
          %p
            A measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            on a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong regular
            if for any measurable subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subset X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt0
            there is a closed subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subset A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\setminus F
            is measurable and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A\setminus F)\lt\epsilon
          %p
            Radon measures on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
            are regular and tight. Regular tight Borel measures are automatically Radon. A regular Borel measure need not be tight.
          %p
            A Borel measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            on a topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
            (alias τ-regular, τ-smooth) if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\mu|(\bigcup_i U_i)=\lim_i |\mu|(U_i)
            for any directed system of open subsets
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i\subset X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation"} continuous valuation
          %p
            If the above condition only holds in the case
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_i U_i=X
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0
              \-additive
            (or weakly τ-additive) measures.
          %p
            Any regular
            = succeed "-additive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
            = succeed "-additive" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            On a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            every Borel measure is regular. More generally, every Borel measure on a
            %span.newWikiWord
              perfectly normal
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/perfectly+normal"} ?
            space is regular.
          %p
            On a complete separable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            every Borel measure is Radon.
          %p Every Baire measure is regular.
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon measure
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
            measure on a regular space is regular. In particular, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive+measure"} τ-additive measure
            on a compact space is Radon.
          %p
            Every tight
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
            measure is Radon.
          %p
            Every Borel measure on a separable metric space X is τ-additive. Moreover, this is true if X is
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                hereditary Lindelöf
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/hereditary+Lindel%C3%B6f"} ?
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%84-additive"} τ-additive
            measure has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
          %h2#extension_properties Extension properties
          %p
            Every tight Baire measure on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+regular"} completely regular
            space admits a unique extension to a Radon measure. More generally, any tight Baire measure on a Hausdorff space has a Radon extension.
          %p
            Every Baire measure on a σ-compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+regular+space"} completely regular space
            has a unique extension to a Radon measure.
          %h2#relation_to_linear_functionals Relation to linear functionals
          %p
            Given a topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to linear functionals on the space of continuous bounded functions on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p For many types of topological spaces and measures this map is bijective, as indicated below.
          %p
            There is a bijection between Baire measures on a topological space and continuous linear functionals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            on continuous bounded functions such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f_n)\to 0
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \to 0
            pointwise and monotonic.
          %p
            There is a bijection between Radon measures on a completely regular topological space and continuous linear functionals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            on continuous bounded functions such that for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt0
            there is a compact subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            such that for any continuous bounded function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            that vanishes on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |L(f)|\le\epsilon\sup|f|
          %p
            There is a bijection between τ-additive Borel measures on a completely regular topological space and continuous linear functionals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            on continuous bounded functions such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f_a)\to0
            for any net
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of bounded continuous functions that decreases to zero pointwise.
          %p
            There is a bijection between positive Borel measures on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact"} locally compact
            topological space that are inner regular on all Borel subsets with respect to compact subsets and positive linear functionals on continuous functions vanishing at infinity.
